# Screen toys: animations and effects, one stanza per program.  The
# play-tests in tools/playtests cover bite, card, life, rain and
# worms.

shot    ttyexp
size    30 80
cap     Two bursts of fifty points each, caught partway through their fall.
cap     Besides -s, -p and -D, -x and -y set the size of each burst, -g the
cap     gravity and -w a wind.
try     ttyexp -s2 -p50
run     ttyexp -s2 -p50
wait    3
snap
wait    2
snap
wait    7

shot    xmas
size    24 80
cap     The reindeer mid-run past the tree, with the greeting across the top.
try     xmas
run     xmas
wait    60
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    rot22
size    24 80
cap     Software rot, demonstrated: the letters of a file come loose a few at
cap     a time and fall down the screen, piling up at the bottom until the
cap     text has drained out of the top.  Give it a file or pipe text in.
cap     This is a still from partway through; it is a moving picture.
try     rot22 DOC/README-CIO
run     builtin cd /dd
wait    1
run     clear
wait    1
run     rot22 DOC/README-CIO
wait    3
snap
wait    12

shot    juggle
size    24 80
cap     The three-ball cascade, `3' in site-swap notation: each ball is
cap     thrown from one hand to the other and caught to be thrown again.
cap     It runs until ^C; this is one frame of the moving picture.
try     juggle -p 3
run     juggle -p 3
wait    3
snap
wait    1
snap
wait    1
snap
wait    1
snap
send    \003
wait    3
